This binding calls unchanged, compiled FlashMLA kernel instantiations from
vllm-project/FlashMLA commit 0eee43b12f034b657133cf2afca6a72ebb6efccf:
https://github.com/vllm-project/FlashMLA/tree/0eee43b12f034b657133cf2afca6a72ebb6efccf

The two headers beneath csrc/kernels are unchanged from that revision. The
headers beneath csrc/cutlass are unchanged from its CUTLASS submodule revision
147f5673d0c1c3dcf66f78d677fd647e4a020219. LICENSE.FlashMLA and LICENSE.CUTLASS
retain the upstream licenses. The headers describe the compiled parameter ABI
and its numeric types; Flare does not compile another copy of the GPU kernels.

Flare supplies the host binding, explicit output/statistics buffers, validation,
and preparation integration. This preserves the upstream kernel arithmetic
while making storage visible to complete-forward compilation. FlashMLA is a
preparation dependency; exported native graphs retain their compiled CUDA code.
